    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **257 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the optional owner `email` field per the spec, following the existing telephone-handling convention. Changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `email` property (`type: string`, `format: email`, `maxLength: 255`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since it's not in the `required` list, it's optional, and the OpenAPI generator emits `getEmail`/`setEmail` on the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** (entity) \u2014 Added an `email` field (`@Column(name = \"email\")`, no `@NotEmpty` since it's optional) with getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it by name in both directions.\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 Added an `email` column to `owners` in all four dialects (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`). Also converted the hsqldb `data.sql` positional owner inserts to an explicit column list so the seed data (which has no email) still loads.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 Added a `normalizeEmail` step mirroring `normalizeTelephone`: when an email is present, it's trimmed, validated against `^[^@\\s]+@[^@\\s]+\\.[^@\\s]+$`, and stored lower-cased; an invalid address returns **400 Bad Request**. Absent email is left untouched.\n\nBehavior matches the three acceptance tests: valid email round-trips lower-cased (`Test.User@Example.COM` \u2192 `test.user@example.com`), an invalid one (`not-an-email`) is rejected with 400, and a missing email is accepted.",
